WEBVTT

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:02.681
I've realized something.

00:00:02.932 --> 00:00:06.602
Until now, Kanzaki,
you've lied about many things.

00:00:07.895 --> 00:00:10.606
About my body and my mind.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.567
You've hidden things from the Divers.

00:00:14.109 --> 00:00:17.071
You probably have many other secrets, too.

00:00:17.655 --> 00:00:18.697
But that's...

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:24.245
I was made from your lies.

00:01:57.546 --> 00:02:00.716
I was made from your lies.

00:02:02.635 --> 00:02:06.764
Even though my brain
is fake and artificial,

00:02:07.222 --> 00:02:09.642
I still love Mom and Ryota.

00:02:10.517 --> 00:02:13.437
These feelings are not fake.

00:02:15.022 --> 00:02:16.649
I want to save them both.

00:02:16.899 --> 00:02:19.985
I want to return this body
to the other me.

00:02:20.152 --> 00:02:24.198
She intends to sacrifice her own life
to put an end to all this.

00:02:25.532 --> 00:02:27.159
But that is my role.

00:02:27.743 --> 00:02:28.827
Tachibana.

00:02:29.453 --> 00:02:31.664
That is not my name.

00:02:31.955 --> 00:02:34.041
There is only one Aiko Tachibana.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.836
Are you sure you want to do this?

00:02:38.003 --> 00:02:41.507
Why are you asking?
Isn't that what you want?

00:02:41.632 --> 00:02:43.801
If we don't hurry, the other me--

00:02:43.884 --> 00:02:45.636
Hold on! I--

00:02:45.719 --> 00:02:47.096
-Kanzaki--
-No!

00:02:49.139 --> 00:02:52.059
I'm not Yuya Kanzaki, either.

00:02:54.603 --> 00:02:56.647
Okay, let's begin.

00:02:57.231 --> 00:02:58.357
Hold on!

00:02:59.149 --> 00:03:01.068
Please don't interfere.

00:03:01.151 --> 00:03:02.194
Sir!

00:03:02.361 --> 00:03:03.529
Dr. Isazu.

00:03:05.739 --> 00:03:06.615
Saho?

00:03:06.698 --> 00:03:10.869
Is it really okay to do this, sir?

00:03:11.662 --> 00:03:14.081
It's been proven
we can establish a link.

00:03:14.623 --> 00:03:15.499
And...

00:03:16.333 --> 00:03:18.419
Yuzuha is my daughter.

00:03:19.795 --> 00:03:20.838
Yuzuha?

00:03:21.422 --> 00:03:23.841
Saho, did you know about this?

00:03:24.425 --> 00:03:25.592
Yes, of course.

00:03:25.718 --> 00:03:30.723
I've been with Yuzuha and Dr. Isazu
for a long time, you know.

00:03:32.766 --> 00:03:36.854
It's only natural that I assist
in restoring Yuzuha's consciousness.

00:03:40.315 --> 00:03:43.944
Okay, Yuzuha. Lend me your strength.

00:04:20.397 --> 00:04:26.028
I believed that my body and my life
would last only until...

00:04:26.904 --> 00:04:28.363
the Burst is ended.

00:04:30.574 --> 00:04:33.285
But, not you. You're...

00:04:46.924 --> 00:04:48.175
<i>Aiko.</i>

00:04:48.258 --> 00:04:49.176
What?

00:04:50.052 --> 00:04:52.888
<i>There's no need to sacrifice yourself.</i>

00:04:53.138 --> 00:04:55.641
<i>You are undoubtedly one of a kind.</i>

00:04:56.308 --> 00:04:57.768
Dr. Isazu?

00:04:57.976 --> 00:05:00.187
Is he controlling the Matter?

00:05:00.854 --> 00:05:04.358
There's no reason for you
to get caught up in his obsession

00:05:04.441 --> 00:05:05.859
and lose your life.

00:05:07.736 --> 00:05:12.658
<i>I can put your life to much better use.</i>

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:16.161
Kanzaki!

00:05:17.204 --> 00:05:18.372
Kanzaki!

00:05:20.666 --> 00:05:23.210
<i>This Matter is from the duplicate bodies</i>

00:05:23.293 --> 00:05:26.547
<i>you created using Cell Assembler Two.</i>

00:05:27.089 --> 00:05:29.758
<i>They just don't have functioning brains.</i>

00:05:29.925 --> 00:05:31.802
<i>They're all my daughter.</i>

00:05:32.594 --> 00:05:36.807
<i>Even now, their minds are connected</i>
<i>to my comatose daughter.</i>

00:05:37.849 --> 00:05:40.227
<i>To return Yuzuha to consciousness,</i>

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:41.728
<i>Aiko Tachibana,</i>

00:05:41.812 --> 00:05:45.315
<i>I must have</i>
<i>your artificial organism brain.</i>

00:05:45.399 --> 00:05:47.067
My brain?

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:48.485
<i>You see,</i>

00:05:48.944 --> 00:05:51.238
<i>the only brain ever regenerated,</i>

00:05:51.446 --> 00:05:55.701
<i>or should I say,</i>
<i>the only successfully created brain...</i>

00:05:56.118 --> 00:05:57.536
<i>is yours.</i>

00:05:57.744 --> 00:06:02.207
<i>I will probe your brain at the</i>
<i>molecular level to discover its secret.</i>

00:06:04.251 --> 00:06:05.544
This is insane!

00:06:06.044 --> 00:06:09.339
So, Yura and Isazu
have been fighting to get her brain?

00:06:10.215 --> 00:06:11.800
So it seems.

00:06:12.092 --> 00:06:15.637
You monsters! Grown men
fighting over a young girl's brain?

00:06:17.389 --> 00:06:21.226
<i>You succeeded in bringing to life</i>

00:06:21.435 --> 00:06:25.564
<i>an artificial organism brain</i>
<i>for the first time in history.</i>

00:06:25.731 --> 00:06:28.859
<i>Is this all recorded in the Yura Notes?</i>

00:06:30.027 --> 00:06:32.195
<i>Tell me! What is the secret?</i>

00:06:40.162 --> 00:06:41.496
Tachibana!

00:06:41.663 --> 00:06:45.959
<i>I won't kill her.</i>
<i>I don't want her to hear this.</i>

00:06:46.043 --> 00:06:47.753
<i>All right, tell me!</i>

00:06:50.422 --> 00:06:52.007
It's Cell Assembler...

00:06:53.216 --> 00:06:54.092
Three.

00:06:54.217 --> 00:06:56.470
What? Three?

00:06:56.553 --> 00:06:58.055
Impossible!

00:06:58.347 --> 00:07:01.141
You mean you upgraded the Cell Assembler?

00:07:01.808 --> 00:07:04.019
Thanks to Cell Assembler Two,

00:07:04.144 --> 00:07:07.522
resilient cells were able to
reproduce rapidly.

00:07:07.648 --> 00:07:09.900
They couldn't be damaged or degraded.

00:07:10.859 --> 00:07:14.655
But, that wasn't enough to make a brain.

00:07:14.821 --> 00:07:15.989
A brain develops

00:07:16.073 --> 00:07:19.117
by eliminating
previously established connections.

00:07:19.701 --> 00:07:22.829
Early on in development,
randomly created connections

00:07:23.288 --> 00:07:25.499
are soon selectively destroyed,

00:07:25.624 --> 00:07:28.293
and a refined network grows.

00:07:28.377 --> 00:07:30.504
<i>I know that!</i>

00:07:30.754 --> 00:07:34.466
<i>Theoretically, artificial reproduction</i>
<i>of a human personality</i>

00:07:34.883 --> 00:07:38.220
<i>capable of controlling</i>
<i>such a highly uncertain process--</i>

00:07:38.303 --> 00:07:39.471
Was impossible.

00:07:40.305 --> 00:07:41.598
Therefore,

00:07:41.723 --> 00:07:45.227
after I accelerated network creation
to be as fast as possible,

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:46.520
I waited...

00:07:47.604 --> 00:07:51.525
<i>until the person</i>
<i>called Aiko Tachibana emerged.</i>

00:07:51.608 --> 00:07:52.943
<i>Impossible!</i>

00:07:53.235 --> 00:07:57.114
<i>That would take as long</i>
<i>as the evolution of life itself!</i>

00:07:57.906 --> 00:08:01.576
As I developed Cell Assembler Two,

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:04.955
I also developed Dream Contact technology.

00:08:05.747 --> 00:08:07.582
<i>Dream Contact?</i>

00:08:07.791 --> 00:08:09.376
Like you said,

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:12.713
brain formation resembles
the evolution of life.

00:08:14.172 --> 00:08:15.674
To proceed naturally,

00:08:16.216 --> 00:08:18.760
<i>an emulation of</i>
<i>infinite possibilities is needed</i>

00:08:18.844 --> 00:08:21.430
<i>to duplicate a mind</i>
<i>with a will of its own.</i>

00:08:22.014 --> 00:08:25.767
<i>I was able to perfectly monitor</i>
<i>the brain activity</i>

00:08:25.851 --> 00:08:28.103
<i>of the original Aiko Tachibana.</i>

00:08:28.353 --> 00:08:30.230
<i>The goal was in sight.</i>

00:08:30.439 --> 00:08:33.900
<i>I repeatedly did the reverse calculations.</i>

00:08:34.526 --> 00:08:39.740
<i>All the unlimited divergent possibilities</i>
<i>cancelled each other out and optimized.</i>

00:08:39.823 --> 00:08:41.742
<i>In a surprisingly short time,</i>

00:08:41.867 --> 00:08:46.496
<i>an artificial brain that could be called</i>
<i>Aiko Tachibana came into existence.</i>

00:08:48.081 --> 00:08:50.959
Your friend is a bit of a mad scientist.

00:08:51.084 --> 00:08:53.545
That mad scientist is our only hope now.

00:08:54.004 --> 00:08:55.922
He can still stop the Burst.

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:00.177
<i>As I'm sure you can see,</i>

00:09:00.761 --> 00:09:02.846
<i>the reinforcements at Camp Toyama</i>

00:09:02.929 --> 00:09:07.559
<i>are leaving the base, and heading out</i>
<i>to incinerate the Malignant Matter Area.</i>

00:09:08.477 --> 00:09:12.105
<i>All Self-Defense Forces branches</i>
<i>are being concentrated</i>

00:09:12.189 --> 00:09:14.566
<i>for a decisive strike</i>
<i>to end the crisis.</i>

00:09:14.649 --> 00:09:16.610
MALIGNANT AREA
TO BE INCINERATED

00:09:21.573 --> 00:09:24.242
<i>Fine!</i>
<i>I acknowledge your godlike abilities!</i>

00:09:24.451 --> 00:09:26.953
<i>But things must return</i>
<i>to where they belong!</i>

00:09:27.037 --> 00:09:30.123
<i>Return gods to the gods!</i>
<i>Return Yuzuha to me!</i>

00:09:30.415 --> 00:09:33.126
Back to the gods with you, Toshihide Yura!

00:09:35.295 --> 00:09:37.255
<i>Know Yuzuha's pain!</i>

00:09:37.839 --> 00:09:40.592
<i>Be punished for preventing</i>
<i>her from waking up!</i>

00:09:51.686 --> 00:09:52.604
Gummi?

00:09:53.105 --> 00:09:54.981
Where am I?

00:09:55.857 --> 00:09:57.651
Is this the other me?

00:10:02.322 --> 00:10:03.281
Who's that?

00:10:04.991 --> 00:10:06.368
A girl?

00:10:06.618 --> 00:10:09.037
Which body should I go back to?

00:10:09.204 --> 00:10:11.915
Why is she crying?

00:10:12.833 --> 00:10:15.627
I want to get out of here. Tell me how.

00:10:15.794 --> 00:10:18.505
Stop it, Dad. Don't hurt Dr. Yura.

00:10:19.798 --> 00:10:22.425
Yura? Hey! Wait!

00:10:22.926 --> 00:10:24.427
Please don't hurt him.

00:10:25.053 --> 00:10:27.430
Hey, wait! What's happening to Kanzaki?

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:29.724
Don't kill him!

00:10:40.819 --> 00:10:43.196
Aiko! Aiko!

00:10:45.198 --> 00:10:46.158
Kazuki.

00:10:46.741 --> 00:10:48.034
Thank goodness.

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:53.999
-Kanzaki!
-This way! Hurry!

00:10:54.833 --> 00:10:55.792
Kanzaki.

00:10:55.876 --> 00:10:57.377
I'm going to jump, Aiko.

00:11:02.674 --> 00:11:04.050
I'll take a magazine.

00:11:04.551 --> 00:11:05.635
Take these stairs.

00:11:08.054 --> 00:11:08.889
Hurry!

00:11:11.349 --> 00:11:13.935
<i>The Self-Defense Forces will attack soon.</i>

00:11:14.519 --> 00:11:18.732
<i>There's no way you can accomplish</i>
<i>what you came to do, Yura.</i>

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:21.902
<i>Give it all up! Get in the shelter!</i>

00:11:22.027 --> 00:11:23.528
<i>Obey me!</i>

00:11:30.785 --> 00:11:31.703
Director!

00:11:32.537 --> 00:11:35.206
All AMBREC companies
announced they'll cancel

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:37.834
our exclusive use
of their technologies.

00:11:37.918 --> 00:11:41.546
If the attack proceeds,
all that science will go abroad.

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:43.548
-Not yet.
-What?

00:11:44.424 --> 00:11:47.010
We can stall this a little bit longer.

00:11:47.135 --> 00:11:48.011
Hori.

00:11:48.762 --> 00:11:49.638
Yes?

00:11:50.263 --> 00:11:52.223
I have a favor to ask you.

00:12:00.982 --> 00:12:02.067
Damn it!

00:12:12.994 --> 00:12:14.079
This must be...

00:12:14.996 --> 00:12:17.582
I'll try to suppress the Matter.

00:12:18.583 --> 00:12:20.251
She's protecting us.

00:12:20.377 --> 00:12:21.419
Protecting us?

00:12:22.003 --> 00:12:23.213
Okay, let's go!

00:12:37.394 --> 00:12:39.104
Is Tachibana okay?

00:12:39.187 --> 00:12:40.480
Is she all right?

00:12:40.563 --> 00:12:42.941
-Yes, she's fine!
-Kanzaki!

00:12:43.525 --> 00:12:46.528
Turn right. It's the last room!
I'll be there soon!

00:12:51.574 --> 00:12:54.536
I will protect...

00:12:55.996 --> 00:12:57.080
Tachibana Aiko!

00:13:02.335 --> 00:13:03.753
Kanzaki!

00:13:04.129 --> 00:13:05.213
Kanzaki!

00:13:14.139 --> 00:13:17.225
This isn't the shelter, is it?

00:13:18.393 --> 00:13:20.020
It's a medicinal warehouse.

00:13:20.687 --> 00:13:22.105
It's pretty sturdy.

00:13:24.107 --> 00:13:29.571
Kanzaki, I saw a girl inside the Matter.

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:31.281
A girl?

00:13:31.948 --> 00:13:34.743
She was a pretty girl with long hair.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:36.494
She wanted to get out,

00:13:36.953 --> 00:13:39.039
and asked which body to go back to.

00:13:41.458 --> 00:13:43.418
Where should I go?

00:13:44.794 --> 00:13:46.588
So, that's what's going on.

00:13:47.338 --> 00:13:50.258
Hey, what are you doing? What's your plan?

00:13:53.053 --> 00:13:56.181
Let's go, Aiko. Let's get to the shelter.

00:13:57.599 --> 00:13:58.767
Aiko!

00:13:59.684 --> 00:14:02.270
I'm sorry, but I'm not going.

00:14:02.353 --> 00:14:05.857
Why not? I don't want you to die!

00:14:09.277 --> 00:14:13.031
Before I met you,
when my arm was grabbed by the Matter...

00:14:13.823 --> 00:14:15.075
I saw a vision.

00:14:28.213 --> 00:14:32.050
There was a happy family.
A traffic accident. The Burst.

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:33.885
I understand it now.

00:14:34.427 --> 00:14:37.055
Those were your memories!

00:14:38.681 --> 00:14:40.392
I want to save you!

00:14:40.517 --> 00:14:42.727
No matter how hard things get,

00:14:43.228 --> 00:14:45.271
I swear I'll be by your side!

00:14:51.611 --> 00:14:54.572
Kazuki, that was not me.

00:14:55.281 --> 00:14:57.075
It's memories of the other me.

00:14:57.158 --> 00:14:58.535
What?

00:14:59.119 --> 00:15:01.955
That wasn't me.

00:15:03.915 --> 00:15:06.584
I can't understand it! How can that be?

00:15:07.293 --> 00:15:08.545
I love...

00:15:09.337 --> 00:15:12.382
I'm in love with you!

00:15:14.676 --> 00:15:16.970
Thank you, but...

00:15:17.053 --> 00:15:18.763
Don't say it!

00:15:24.394 --> 00:15:25.562
Give me your gun.

00:15:27.313 --> 00:15:30.525
This will cause an explosion
when ignited.

00:15:31.025 --> 00:15:33.987
It'll blow a path
through the door and the Matter.

00:15:34.612 --> 00:15:35.780
Are you crazy?

00:15:36.698 --> 00:15:39.325
Fine. Shoot it, then.

00:15:39.534 --> 00:15:41.953
Get down as soon as you pull the trigger.

00:15:42.787 --> 00:15:44.205
Kanzaki!

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:46.499
I can sense it!

00:15:47.083 --> 00:15:50.753
I know you have feelings for Aiko, too!

00:15:51.045 --> 00:15:52.422
But you'll still do it?

00:15:52.881 --> 00:15:55.925
You still plan on turning her
into the Matter?

00:15:56.009 --> 00:15:58.761
Will you toss her aside
and tell her to die?

00:16:03.683 --> 00:16:04.684
Kazuki.

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:09.689
If you love me, then save them.

00:16:10.356 --> 00:16:11.566
Aiko.

00:16:12.233 --> 00:16:14.611
Not my body or my mind.

00:16:15.612 --> 00:16:17.155
Save my Mom and Ryota.

00:16:17.906 --> 00:16:20.575
My heart demands it!

00:16:49.938 --> 00:16:54.817
Tank and artillery battalions will
commence firing at 8:00 p.m. as planned.

00:17:02.242 --> 00:17:05.411
There are numerous
civilian trespassers in the Area.

00:17:07.789 --> 00:17:09.749
All units, hold your fire!

00:17:27.392 --> 00:17:28.893
You really are amazing.

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.233
Explain yourself, Nanbara!

00:17:36.568 --> 00:17:40.655
I exercised my right as Director
to lift the Malignant Area blockade.

00:17:41.239 --> 00:17:42.282
For what reason?!

00:17:43.032 --> 00:17:46.035
Since Matter activity
in Area Four has ceased,

00:17:46.202 --> 00:17:49.455
I decided that securing samples
there took priority.

00:17:50.623 --> 00:17:51.958
Damn you!

00:17:52.542 --> 00:17:55.253
I was given
complete authority over the Area.

00:17:56.045 --> 00:17:58.214
That's enough!
Recall those Divers!

00:17:58.464 --> 00:18:01.134
You're relieved of your post immediately!

00:18:13.563 --> 00:18:18.192
If you don't want to go down with her,
tell me everything she knows!

00:18:18.276 --> 00:18:20.028
Write a report immediately!

00:18:26.868 --> 00:18:28.202
<i>Hello? Who is this?</i>

00:18:28.328 --> 00:18:32.081
<i>Nanbara asked me to call.</i>
<i>My name is Hori. I work for her.</i>

00:18:32.665 --> 00:18:33.833
You work for her?

00:18:33.958 --> 00:18:35.043
<i>I have a message.</i>

00:18:35.293 --> 00:18:38.254
<i>The attack on the Area has been postponed.</i>

00:18:38.421 --> 00:18:39.505
Really?

00:18:39.631 --> 00:18:41.633
<i>The Director has bought you time.</i>

00:18:41.883 --> 00:18:43.676
I see. What happened to her?

00:18:44.552 --> 00:18:48.640
<i>She has sacrificed everything</i>
<i>she worked for, her entire career,</i>

00:18:48.723 --> 00:18:50.099
<i>to stop the attack.</i>

00:18:50.183 --> 00:18:52.352
What? Don't tell me...

00:18:52.894 --> 00:18:56.564
<i>She constantly spoke about</i>
<i>the interests of the nation.</i>

00:18:56.773 --> 00:19:00.026
<i>I've never seen anyone sacrifice</i>
<i>so much for something</i>

00:19:00.318 --> 00:19:01.152
<i>so abstract.</i>

00:19:01.986 --> 00:19:05.490
The attack would only make
the Burst worse.

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:08.534
Your boss did the right thing.

00:19:09.243 --> 00:19:10.578
<i>She'll be rewarded.</i>

00:19:13.706 --> 00:19:16.292
The attack has been postponed.
Inform Yura.

00:19:16.417 --> 00:19:17.543
Impossible.

00:19:18.628 --> 00:19:21.297
We can see Research Facility Two.

00:19:21.547 --> 00:19:25.551
But if we contact them,
Isazu will find out, too.

00:19:32.016 --> 00:19:32.892
I know!

00:19:39.482 --> 00:19:40.358
What's that?

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:44.070
Is it broken?

00:19:44.153 --> 00:19:46.072
-It's saying something.
-What?

00:19:46.489 --> 00:19:48.282
"Yuya, come in."

00:19:49.367 --> 00:19:50.576
Kurose?

00:19:51.244 --> 00:19:52.954
Visible light communication?

00:19:54.747 --> 00:19:55.748
We got through!

00:19:57.792 --> 00:19:59.001
<i>He's answering!</i>

00:19:59.085 --> 00:20:00.378
I'll read it.

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:05.758
"Cut the link between Yuzuha
and her duplicate bodies."

00:20:06.134 --> 00:20:07.009
What?

00:20:07.218 --> 00:20:08.636
Link?

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:11.806
The comatose girl
is linked to her duplicate bodies?

00:20:12.432 --> 00:20:15.601
Isazu is trying to return Yuzuha
to consciousness.

00:20:15.685 --> 00:20:19.772
He's trying to physically sync
her with her duplicate bodies' brains.

00:20:20.356 --> 00:20:24.527
<i>None of them succeeded.</i>
<i>So why were they still connected?</i>

00:20:25.111 --> 00:20:27.363
Then, how do we cut the link?

00:20:27.947 --> 00:20:29.365
At Kiryu Hospital.

00:20:29.574 --> 00:20:32.827
It means we sneak in
right under Isazu's nose.

00:20:35.413 --> 00:20:37.665
Three blocks to Primary Point.

00:20:37.874 --> 00:20:40.126
But no sign of
the two people we need.

00:20:40.501 --> 00:20:42.128
-Seri!
-Damn!

00:20:51.554 --> 00:20:52.472
Kaede!

00:20:55.641 --> 00:20:57.477
If they're lost...

00:20:58.519 --> 00:21:01.814
Then we'll just have to bring them
to their objective.

00:21:03.024 --> 00:21:05.276
There's a purpose to what we're doing.

00:21:09.322 --> 00:21:10.239
Right!

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:12.617
RECALL THE SELF-DEFENSE FORCES!

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:15.495
The existence of your company
and AMBREC itself

00:21:15.578 --> 00:21:17.246
is in the national interest.

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:18.998
There is still hope.

00:21:20.333 --> 00:21:21.626
Yura...

00:21:22.126 --> 00:21:24.003
Yura!

00:21:24.587 --> 00:21:26.088
Stop it!

00:21:26.172 --> 00:21:28.758
Don't interfere, Takehara!

00:21:28.883 --> 00:21:31.135
This is an official operation!

00:21:35.264 --> 00:21:38.726
This is Primary Point.

00:21:39.310 --> 00:21:40.978
-What?
-Here?

00:21:41.687 --> 00:21:45.107
The multipurpose surgical installation
ALSUS is in here.

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:48.236
Let's go.

00:21:56.869 --> 00:21:59.789
I know this place.

00:22:00.456 --> 00:22:03.167
I've seen it many times
in my dreams.

00:22:20.935 --> 00:22:24.021
This is ALSUS?

00:23:57.782 --> 00:23:59.950
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
